# Semantic colors (mandatory)

All **semantic** UI color (red/green/blue/yellow/orange status tints) MUST come from the shared token system — never invent new Tailwind hue classes in components.

## Single source of truth

| File | Role |
|------|------|
| `frontend/src/lib/semantic-colors.ts` | **Only** place raw `rose-*` / `emerald-*` / etc. class strings may be defined |
| `frontend/src/lib/style-maps.ts` | Domain maps: `STATUS_STYLES`, `SEVERITY_COLORS`, `VERDICT_STYLES`, `PROVIDER_OK`, … |

```tsx
import { SEMANTIC_COLORS, PROVIDER_OK, SEVERITY_COLORS } from "@/lib/style-maps";

// ✅ tinted panel
className={SEMANTIC_COLORS.rose.inset}

// ✅ status dot + label (same green as Provider “Operational”)
className={PROVIDER_OK.text}

// ❌ never in components
className="text-rose-600 dark:text-rose-400"
className="border-emerald-200 bg-emerald-50"
```

## Hue meanings (fixed palette)

| Hue | Meaning |
|-----|---------|
| `rose` | critical, error, down, fail |
| `emerald` | success, operational, pass (`PROVIDER_OK`) |
| `amber` | warning, degraded, account-side |
| `sky` | info, maintenance, chart bars |
| `yellow` | trending down, config |
| `orange` | rate limit, partial outage |

Neutrals (`zinc-*`, `--background`, `--accent`) are fine outside this system.

## Adding a new semantic color

1. Add or extend a hue in `semantic-colors.ts` only.
2. Wire through `style-maps.ts` if it maps to product semantics.
3. Run `npm run lint:colors` in `frontend/`.

## Enforcement

`npm run lint:colors` fails the build if components contain forbidden hue utilities. Fix violations by importing tokens — do not disable the check.
